1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,649
Mastery evidence.

2
00:00:01,649 --> 00:00:04,556
You have learned Bash scripting: variables,

3
00:00:04,556 --> 00:00:04,962
tests,

4
00:00:04,962 --> 00:00:05,368
loops,

5
00:00:05,368 --> 00:00:05,773
pipes,

6
00:00:05,773 --> 00:00:06,788
error handling,

7
00:00:06,788 --> 00:00:07,396
security,

8
00:00:07,396 --> 00:00:08,545
and safe deploys.

9
00:00:08,545 --> 00:00:09,695
Now you prove it.

10
00:00:10,245 --> 00:00:13,066
Mastery means someone else could check your work.

11
00:00:13,066 --> 00:00:14,852
So this lesson gives you a lab,

12
00:00:14,852 --> 00:00:16,752
a checker that says pass or fail,

13
00:00:16,752 --> 00:00:19,055
and a report that shows how you thought.

14
00:00:19,605 --> 00:00:24,405
I will build the lab, fix the first broken script live, and leave the other three to you.

15
00:00:26,455 --> 00:00:31,127
Meet a small team's toolbox. Four Bash scripts, each one broken on purpose.

16
00:00:31,677 --> 00:00:34,365
A checker prints pass or fail for four checks.

17
00:00:34,915 --> 00:00:38,648
One: archive dot S H must cope with a space in a file name.

18
00:00:39,198 --> 00:00:43,444
Two: backup dot S H must fail, loudly, when the folder is missing.

19
00:00:43,994 --> 00:00:47,727
Three: count errors dot S H must count lines, not words.

20
00:00:48,277 --> 00:00:51,413
Four: setup dot S H must be safe to run twice.

21
00:00:51,963 --> 00:00:55,312
Your mission: four pass lines, with proof for every fix.

22
00:00:57,362 --> 00:01:01,565
Before we start, here is where everything lives. It is also in the description.

23
00:01:02,115 --> 00:01:07,789
The repository is git hub dot com, slash it dash waves, slash dev ops dash A I.

24
00:01:08,339 --> 00:01:11,321
The lab is one file: lab forty-six dot S H,

25
00:01:11,321 --> 00:01:13,539
in the academy slash lab folder.

26
00:01:13,539 --> 00:01:18,878
Your report template and install notes are in academy slash lesson forty-six.

27
00:01:19,428 --> 00:01:21,309
Install it in three steps.

28
00:01:21,309 --> 00:01:22,828
Clone the repository.

29
00:01:22,828 --> 00:01:24,347
Go to the lab folder.

30
00:01:24,347 --> 00:01:28,687
Install the script into slash U S R slash local slash S bin.

31
00:01:29,237 --> 00:01:31,258
Three commands run everything.

32
00:01:31,258 --> 00:01:33,077
Lab up builds the problems.

33
00:01:33,077 --> 00:01:35,705
Lab check prints pass or fail for each.

34
00:01:35,705 --> 00:01:37,322
Lab down removes it all.

35
00:01:37,872 --> 00:01:39,269
Lab is a short name.

36
00:01:39,269 --> 00:01:41,085
Source the shortcuts file,

37
00:01:41,085 --> 00:01:42,412
and it runs sue do,

38
00:01:42,412 --> 00:01:43,948
lab forty-six dot S H,

39
00:01:43,948 --> 00:01:44,507
for you.

40
00:01:45,057 --> 00:01:48,334
You need an Ubuntu virtual machine with root and bash.

41
00:01:48,334 --> 00:01:50,155
Shell Check is a useful extra.

42
00:01:50,155 --> 00:01:52,097
Run it only in your own machine.

43
00:01:54,447 --> 00:01:55,379
Now for real.

44
00:01:55,379 --> 00:01:57,458
I have cloned the repository,

45
00:01:57,458 --> 00:02:00,683
and the lab files are in a folder called lab.

46
00:02:00,683 --> 00:02:01,328
Type: CD,

47
00:02:01,328 --> 00:02:01,615
lab.

48
00:02:02,165 --> 00:02:04,320
List what is here. Type: L S.

49
00:02:04,870 --> 00:02:07,916
The lab script and the shortcuts file.

50
00:02:07,916 --> 00:02:09,439
Install the script.

51
00:02:09,439 --> 00:02:10,481
Type: sue do,

52
00:02:10,481 --> 00:02:11,122
install,

53
00:02:11,122 --> 00:02:11,683
dash m,

54
00:02:11,683 --> 00:02:12,966
seven five five,

55
00:02:12,966 --> 00:02:14,729
lab forty-six dot S H,

56
00:02:14,729 --> 00:02:17,615
slash U S R slash local slash S bin.

57
00:02:17,615 --> 00:02:21,062
Dash m seven five five makes it executable.

58
00:02:21,612 --> 00:02:26,284
Load the short names. Type: source, shortcuts forty-six dot S H.

59
00:02:26,834 --> 00:02:28,860
Build the lab. Type: lab up.

60
00:02:31,410 --> 00:02:33,992
Now ask the checker. Type: lab check.

61
00:02:35,542 --> 00:02:39,702
Four FAIL lines. That is your starting point. Copy them into your report.

62
00:02:41,752 --> 00:02:43,501
Keep four notes for every fault.

63
00:02:44,051 --> 00:02:47,017
One: the symptom, in the exact words of the error.

64
00:02:47,567 --> 00:02:49,999
Two: the cause, and the command that proved it.

65
00:02:50,549 --> 00:02:52,831
Three: the fix. One change only.

66
00:02:53,381 --> 00:02:55,813
Four: the proof, the output after the fix.

67
00:02:56,363 --> 00:02:58,518
Notes turn a lucky fix into evidence.

68
00:03:00,568 --> 00:03:01,303
Fault one,

69
00:03:01,303 --> 00:03:01,671
live.

70
00:03:01,671 --> 00:03:06,818
The checker says archive dot S H does not cope with a space in a name.

71
00:03:06,818 --> 00:03:08,656
Go to the scripts folder.

72
00:03:08,656 --> 00:03:09,318
Type: CD,

73
00:03:09,318 --> 00:03:10,053
slash opt,

74
00:03:10,053 --> 00:03:11,523
slash lab forty-six,

75
00:03:11,523 --> 00:03:12,259
slash bin.

76
00:03:12,809 --> 00:03:15,422
Run the script the way the checker does,

77
00:03:15,422 --> 00:03:17,643
with a file name that has a space,

78
00:03:17,643 --> 00:03:18,296
in quotes.

79
00:03:18,296 --> 00:03:20,386
Type: dot slash archive dot S H,

80
00:03:20,386 --> 00:03:21,235
and the name.

81
00:03:21,785 --> 00:03:22,410
Note one,

82
00:03:22,410 --> 00:03:24,355
the symptom: two C P errors,

83
00:03:24,355 --> 00:03:27,203
and then the script says archived anyway.

84
00:03:27,203 --> 00:03:29,565
It reported success while failing.

85
00:03:29,565 --> 00:03:31,649
Now find the cause with proof,

86
00:03:31,649 --> 00:03:32,552
do not guess.

87
00:03:32,552 --> 00:03:33,802
Type: bash dash x,

88
00:03:33,802 --> 00:03:34,914
archive dot S H,

89
00:03:34,914 --> 00:03:36,164
and the same name.

90
00:03:36,714 --> 00:03:37,330
Note two,

91
00:03:37,330 --> 00:03:38,015
the cause.

92
00:03:38,015 --> 00:03:39,453
Look at the C P line.

93
00:03:39,453 --> 00:03:42,193
The shell split the name into two words,

94
00:03:42,193 --> 00:03:43,905
daily and notes dot text.

95
00:03:43,905 --> 00:03:46,028
The variable was not in quotes.

96
00:03:46,028 --> 00:03:47,671
This trace is the proof.

97
00:03:47,671 --> 00:03:48,425
Note three,

98
00:03:48,425 --> 00:03:49,178
one change.

99
00:03:49,178 --> 00:03:49,863
Type: sed,

100
00:03:49,863 --> 00:03:50,342
dash i,

101
00:03:50,342 --> 00:03:54,314
and the substitution that puts quotes around dollar S R C.

102
00:03:54,864 --> 00:03:55,551
Note four,

103
00:03:55,551 --> 00:03:56,239
the proof.

104
00:03:56,239 --> 00:03:57,682
Run the script again,

105
00:03:57,682 --> 00:03:59,332
with the very same name,

106
00:03:59,332 --> 00:04:02,288
and watch what the C P step does this time.

107
00:04:02,288 --> 00:04:04,488
Type: dot slash archive dot S H,

108
00:04:04,488 --> 00:04:05,381
and the name.

109
00:04:06,131 --> 00:04:11,721
One file copied, and archived printed once. Now ask the checker. Type: lab check.

110
00:04:12,271 --> 00:04:12,857
One PASS,

111
00:04:12,857 --> 00:04:13,573
three FAIL.

112
00:04:13,573 --> 00:04:14,549
One fault down,

113
00:04:14,549 --> 00:04:15,265
one change,

114
00:04:15,265 --> 00:04:15,981
with proof.

115
00:04:15,981 --> 00:04:18,585
Now it is your turn for the other three.

116
00:04:20,635 --> 00:04:24,411
Your report has five parts. The template is in the lesson folder.

117
00:04:24,961 --> 00:04:27,094
Setup: the checker output at the start.

118
00:04:27,644 --> 00:04:29,266
Each fault, with its four notes.

119
00:04:29,816 --> 00:04:32,973
The final checker output, all four lines saying pass.

120
00:04:33,523 --> 00:04:34,651
Where you got stuck,

121
00:04:34,651 --> 00:04:35,836
and what unstuck you.

122
00:04:35,836 --> 00:04:38,600
Honest notes are worth more than a perfect story.

123
00:04:39,150 --> 00:04:41,220
And the cleanup proof, which we do next.

124
00:04:43,170 --> 00:04:46,221
Your three faults. No spoilers, only directions.

125
00:04:46,771 --> 00:04:51,733
Check two: backup dot S H prints finished even when the folder is missing.

126
00:04:51,733 --> 00:04:53,678
Run it with a missing folder,

127
00:04:53,678 --> 00:04:56,093
then ask what exit code it returned.

128
00:04:56,093 --> 00:04:57,568
Read about set dash e,

129
00:04:57,568 --> 00:04:58,037
dash u,

130
00:04:58,037 --> 00:04:58,909
and pipefail.

131
00:04:59,459 --> 00:05:02,527
Check three: count errors dot S H prints four,

132
00:05:02,527 --> 00:05:04,929
but only three log lines have ERROR.

133
00:05:04,929 --> 00:05:08,330
A for loop over a command substitution reads words,

134
00:05:08,330 --> 00:05:08,997
not lines.

135
00:05:08,997 --> 00:05:10,531
Which loop reads lines?

136
00:05:11,081 --> 00:05:13,530
Check four: run setup dot S H twice,

137
00:05:13,530 --> 00:05:15,503
then look at the config file.

138
00:05:15,503 --> 00:05:18,224
What makes adding a line safe to repeat?

139
00:05:18,224 --> 00:05:19,380
Think idempotent.

140
00:05:19,930 --> 00:05:22,977
Shell Check can point at faults one and three.

141
00:05:22,977 --> 00:05:25,096
Same method every time: symptom,

142
00:05:25,096 --> 00:05:25,494
check,

143
00:05:25,494 --> 00:05:26,421
fix one thing,

144
00:05:26,421 --> 00:05:26,885
verify.

145
00:05:28,935 --> 00:05:32,327
When you finish, clean up, and prove it. Type: lab down.

146
00:05:33,877 --> 00:05:39,402
Proof one: is the lab folder gone? Type: L S, slash opt, slash lab forty-six.

147
00:05:39,952 --> 00:05:42,064
No such file or directory.

148
00:05:42,064 --> 00:05:44,258
Proof two: count it in opt.

149
00:05:44,258 --> 00:05:45,070
Type: L S,

150
00:05:45,070 --> 00:05:45,882
slash opt,

151
00:05:45,882 --> 00:05:46,288
pipe,

152
00:05:46,288 --> 00:05:47,263
grep dash c,

153
00:05:47,263 --> 00:05:48,400
lab forty-six.

154
00:05:48,950 --> 00:05:49,386
Zero.

155
00:05:49,386 --> 00:05:52,261
Now remove the lab script itself.

156
00:05:52,261 --> 00:05:53,394
Type: sue do,

157
00:05:53,394 --> 00:05:53,742
R M,

158
00:05:53,742 --> 00:05:59,318
slash U S R slash local slash S bin slash lab forty-six dot S H.

159
00:05:59,868 --> 00:06:03,065
Proof three: is anything left in S bin?

160
00:06:03,065 --> 00:06:03,884
Type: L S,

161
00:06:03,884 --> 00:06:06,834
slash U S R slash local slash S bin,

162
00:06:06,834 --> 00:06:07,244
pipe,

163
00:06:07,244 --> 00:06:07,572
W C,

164
00:06:07,572 --> 00:06:08,146
dash l.

165
00:06:08,696 --> 00:06:12,664
Zero. Everything is removed. Paste these proofs into your report.

166
00:06:14,714 --> 00:06:18,639
Here is how your work is judged. Six points, and you need all six.

167
00:06:19,189 --> 00:06:21,024
The checker shows four pass lines.

168
00:06:21,574 --> 00:06:24,774
Every fault has a symptom, a cause, a fix, and a proof.

169
00:06:25,324 --> 00:06:27,073
You changed one thing at a time.

170
00:06:27,623 --> 00:06:30,439
The report is complete, including where you got stuck.

171
00:06:30,989 --> 00:06:33,336
The cleanup proof shows nothing left behind.

172
00:06:33,886 --> 00:06:36,275
You ran it only in your own virtual machine.

173
00:06:36,825 --> 00:06:38,447
To pass, you need all six.

174
00:06:40,497 --> 00:06:46,364
Your turn, in your own Ubuntu virtual machine. Take your time. Mastery is slow and exact.

175
00:06:46,914 --> 00:06:49,687
One: clone the repository and install the lab.

176
00:06:50,237 --> 00:06:53,053
Two: run lab up, and save the checker output.

177
00:06:53,603 --> 00:06:56,824
Three: fix the three remaining faults, with four notes each.

178
00:06:57,374 --> 00:06:59,486
Four: write the report from the template.

179
00:07:00,036 --> 00:07:03,215
Five: run the checker. All four lines must say pass.

180
00:07:03,765 --> 00:07:05,728
Six: clean up, and paste the proof.

181
00:07:06,278 --> 00:07:08,112
Pause the video, and begin now.

182
00:07:23,662 --> 00:07:24,537
Quick check.

183
00:07:25,087 --> 00:07:27,540
Which option shows each command a script runs?

184
00:07:28,090 --> 00:07:29,797
What are the four notes for a fault?

185
00:07:30,347 --> 00:07:32,267
What makes a script safe to run twice?

186
00:07:32,817 --> 00:07:34,374
What proves your cleanup worked?

187
00:07:34,924 --> 00:07:37,656
Mastery evidence covered: M C zero five,

188
00:07:37,656 --> 00:07:40,047
building on objectives one to nine,

189
00:07:40,047 --> 00:07:42,369
in the Bash scripting masterclass.

190
00:07:42,919 --> 00:07:44,989
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

